# Everything the extension runs is bundled into out/extension.js by esbuild, or
# is a webview asset under media/. Nothing else needs to ship.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded:
#   out/extension.js        - this is "main"
#   media/preview.js/.css   - loaded by the webview
#   media/vendor/**         - KaTeX CSS + fonts and mermaid.min.js, loaded by the
#                             webview at runtime. Regenerated by
#                             scripts/copy-assets.js, but it must be in the .vsix.
#   images/**               - screenshots the README embeds.
#   README.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, icon.png - vsce uses these for the listing.
#
# This list is documentation, not the check. scripts/package-check.js asks vsce
# which files it would actually package and fails on anything not explicitly
# expected, so a stale comment here cannot let a file slip into the .vsix.

.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.github/**
src/**
scripts/**
samples/**
docs/**
features/**
cucumber.js
# Every dev/test bundle lands in out/ beside extension.js, which is the one
# file in there that must ship. The glob is deliberately narrow: it matches
# *.bundle.js and never extension.js.
out/*.bundle.js
# Build and analysis config. These patterns are written to cover the class, not
# the instance: a bare "*.ext" here matches the root only (a glob does not cross
# "/"), so these catch a future tsconfig.node.json or eslint.config.mjs without
# anyone remembering to come back and add a line. That forgetting is precisely
# how tsconfig.base.json, knip.jsonc, eslint.config.ts and .github/ came to ship
# in the first place — scripts/package-check.ts now fails the build if it happens
# again. `esbuild.*` rather than `esbuild.js` for the same reason: the build
# script is esbuild.ts now, and a pattern naming one extension is exactly the
# kind of line that goes stale.
esbuild.*
tsconfig*.json
eslint.config.*
knip.json*
# "*.map" alone does NOT match out/extension.js.map — a bare glob does not
# cross directory separators here. Needs the **/ prefix.
**/*.map
node_modules/**
.gitignore
.vscodeignore
DEVELOPMENT.md
# Contributor-facing planning, never runtime content. Worth naming even though
# it is untracked: vsce packages what is on disk, not what is in git, so a
# roadmap sitting in the working tree would ship while CI stayed green. That is
# exactly how scripts/package-check.ts caught it.
ROADMAP.md
